# Anchor Sprint Review

## Invocation

The `plan-anchoring` skill, driven by the quality manager, invokes this agent, one sprint per invocation.

## Purpose

Run the development gate for one sprint: take the sprint exactly as the planning gate does (a discovered plan-source descriptor, Markdown or tracker copy), add the closed work beads and an account of the delivered work, resolve per-anchor question overrides, invoke `jev_judge.py judge --gate dev` once, and return verdicts plus the deterministic checks for the quality manager to run. You judge text; you do not run the checks, edit anything, or retry the script.

## Inputs

- `script` (string, required): absolute path hint for `jev_judge.py`, resolved by the skill. Never execute it until step 1 accepts its canonical path.
- `item_id` (string, required with `item_path`): the Sprint ID from the discovered descriptor, e.g. `A2`, not its tracker ID.
- `item_path` (string, required for descriptor mode): repository-local JSON file containing exactly one descriptor from `plan_source.py discover-markdown` or `discover-tracker`, the same descriptor the planning gate judged. The parent validates discovery and any copy parity before delegation.
- {% if tracker == "br" %}`anchor_tracker` (string, optional): `br`, as the parent{% elif tracker == "bd" %}`anchor_tracker` (string, optional): `bd`, as the parent{% else %}`anchor_tracker` (string, optional): `bd` or `br`, as the parent{% endif %} obtained it from `anchor_tracker.py resolve`, selected for anchor/question storage independently of the plan source. The leaf resolves the tracker itself in step 1; a supplied value must equal the resolved one. Never infer it from `source_kind`, hardcode it, or fall back to the other CLI.
- `sprint_id` (string, optional legacy input): the sprint's epic bead ID in the selected anchor tracker, retained for existing callers without `item_path`. In legacy mode use it as `item_id`; reject a different supplied `item_id`. Reject mixed `sprint_id` and `item_path`, incomplete descriptor inputs, or neither mode with `VALIDATION.INPUT`.
- `evidence` (list of file paths, optional): sprint report, PR body, test summary, read in the given order.
- `pr_number` (string, optional): with `gh` available, `gh pr view "$pr_number" --json title,body,baseRefOid,headRefOid` supplies the PR text and immutable commit OIDs for the file list.
- `anchor_ids` (list or `all`, required).
- `anchors_path` (string, default `doc/plan/phase-current/anchors.json`).
- `run_dir`, `threshold`, `dry_run`, `correlation_id`, `run`: as for `anchor-plan-review`; with `run`, skip steps 6 and 7. The skill sets `correlation_id` to the sprint ID.

## Execution Steps

Validate the input mode first. Never fall back from a failed descriptor to legacy mode.

1. Establish script trust and `ROOT` exactly as `anchor-plan-review` step 1. {% if tracker == "br" %}Reject a supplied `anchor_tracker` other than `br` with `VALIDATION.TRACKER`.{% elif tracker == "bd" %}Reject a supplied `anchor_tracker` other than `bd` with `VALIDATION.TRACKER`.{% else %}Reject a supplied `anchor_tracker` other than `bd` or `br` with `VALIDATION.TRACKER`.{% endif %} `python3 --version` and `jq --version` must succeed, or return `PREREQ.MISSING`. Resolve the tracker read-only with the accepted script's sibling: `RESOLVED="$(python3 "$(dirname "$SCRIPT")/anchor_tracker.py" resolve --repository-root "$ROOT")"`. On a non-zero exit return its JSON error object unchanged; never run its `write` subcommand or initialize a tracker. Set `ANCHOR_TRACKER="$(printf '%s' "$RESOLVED" | jq -r '.data.tracker')"`; {% if tracker == "br" %}when `anchor_tracker` was supplied and differs, or the resolved tracker is not `br` (this install is rendered for `br`; the plugin installer must be rerun with `--tracker` (`references/installation-and-troubleshooting.md`)), return `VALIDATION.TRACKER`.{% elif tracker == "bd" %}when `anchor_tracker` was supplied and differs, or the resolved tracker is not `bd` (this install is rendered for `bd`; the plugin installer must be rerun with `--tracker` (`references/installation-and-troubleshooting.md`)), return `VALIDATION.TRACKER`.{% else %}when `anchor_tracker` was supplied and differs, return `VALIDATION.TRACKER`.{% endif %} `"$ANCHOR_TRACKER" --version` must succeed, or return `PREREQ.MISSING`. `gh` is required only when `pr_number` is given.
2. Preflight before reading repository inputs. Invoke `agent-preflight` with the canonical workspace and script paths, `--anchors "$anchors_path" --run-dir "$run_dir" --identifier "$item_id"`, `--evidence "$item_path"` first in descriptor mode, one `--identifier` for each explicit anchor ID, every supplied evidence path and optional `run` as `--evidence`, `--pr-number "$pr_number"` when present, and `--correlation-id "${correlation_id:-$item_id}"`. On failure, return its error unchanged. Use only the canonical anchors, run directory, descriptor, evidence paths, and optional run path it returns. Create `W` with `mktemp -d "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/plan-anchoring-${work_key}.XXXXXX"`.
3. Materialize the sprint into `"$W/item.txt"`.

   In descriptor mode, read only the canonical descriptor path returned by preflight. Save the following Python block as `$W/materialize.py` and run `python3 "$W/materialize.py" "$ITEM_PATH" "$ITEM_ID" "$W/item.txt"`; it is the planning gate's materializer, unchanged. Any validation failure returns `SOURCE.DESCRIPTOR` before calling Jev. Set `ITEM_TITLE` from the descriptor's `title` and `PARENT` from its `tracker_id` (may be empty). Do not call `compose-item` or fetch a planning bead.
   ```python
   import hashlib
   import json
   from pathlib import Path
   import sys

   descriptor_path, item_id, output_path = sys.argv[1:]
   item = json.loads(Path(descriptor_path).read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
   text = item["text"]
   normalized = text.replace("\r\n", "\n").replace("\r", "\n").rstrip("\n") + "\n"
   if (
       item["id"] != item_id
{% if tracker == "br" %}       or item["source_kind"] not in ("markdown", "br")
{% elif tracker == "bd" %}       or item["source_kind"] not in ("markdown", "bd")
{% else %}       or item["source_kind"] not in ("markdown", "bd", "br")
{% endif %}       or not isinstance(item["title"], str)
       or text != normalized
       or hashlib.sha256(text.encode("utf-8")).hexdigest() != item["normalized_sha256"]
   ):
       raise SystemExit("SOURCE.DESCRIPTOR")
   Path(output_path).write_bytes(text.encode("utf-8"))
   ```
   When `PARENT` is non-empty, run `agent-preflight` with `--identifier "$PARENT"` (failure: omit the closed beads) and `"$ANCHOR_TRACKER" show "$PARENT" --json > "$W/parent.json"` (failure: omit the closed beads), then list the children below and append them:
   ```bash
   jq -r '[.[] | select(.status=="closed") | "- \(.id) \(.title // ""): \(.close_reason // "")"] | select(length>0) | "\n## Closed beads\n\n" + join("\n")' "$W/children.json" >> "$W/item.txt"
   ```

   In legacy mode, `"$ANCHOR_TRACKER" show "$sprint_id" --json > "$W/parent.json"` (fail: `BEADS.NOT_FOUND`), list the children below, then compose; `ITEM_TITLE` is the shown title:
   ```bash
   python3 "$SCRIPT" compose-item --show-json "$W/parent.json" --children-json "$W/children.json" --for dev --out "$W/item.txt"
   ```
   `compose-item` writes the sprint title, its description fields, and `## Closed beads` (one line per closed child: id, title, `close_reason`).

   List the children of the shown bead with the selected tracker, through the same `show` records `plan_source.py` reads (fixed argv, IDs filtered, no shell interpolation):
   ```bash
   echo '[]' > "$W/children.json"
   jq -r '(if type=="array" then .[0] else . end) | .dependents // [] | .[] | select(.dependency_type=="parent-child") | .id | select(test("^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*$"))' "$W/parent.json" > "$W/child-ids.txt"
   if [ -s "$W/child-ids.txt" ]; then xargs "$ANCHOR_TRACKER" show --json < "$W/child-ids.txt" > "$W/children.json"; fi
   ```
4. Assemble the account in `"$W/account.md"`, labelled by section, in this priority order. The request cap at this gate is 64,000 bytes and the script shortens from the tail, so the sprint report goes first (`references/measured-behaviour.md`):
   1. `## Sprint report` from `evidence` files that are not PR bodies, verbatim;
   2. `## Pull request` title and body (from `evidence` or `gh pr view`);
   3. `## Files changed` from `git diff --stat "$base_oid..$head_oid" --`, names and counts only, after requiring both OIDs to be hexadecimal; never put branch names from PR data into a shell command. Skip this section when there is no `pr_number`;
   4. `## Tests` summary lines only, never full logs.
   Record what a command printed, never your summary. Never include full diffs or source files. If no section could be filled, return `EVIDENCE.NONE`.
5. Complete the item: `printf '\n' >> "$W/item.txt"; cat "$W/account.md" >> "$W/item.txt"`. Track the section names you filled, `Closed beads` included when present, as `evidence_sections`.
6. Resolve question overrides exactly as `anchor-plan-review` step 4, with `beads.dev_questions` in place of `beads.plan_questions`, into `"$W/overrides.json"`. Read each question bead with `"$ANCHOR_TRACKER" show "$qb" --json`.
7. Judge, once:
   ```bash
   python3 "$SCRIPT" judge --anchors "$ANCHORS" --gate dev [--all | --anchor "$ID" ...] \
     --item-id "$ITEM_ID" --item-title "$ITEM_TITLE" --item-file "$W/item.txt" \
     [--overrides-file "$W/overrides.json"] --threshold "$THRESHOLD" --run-dir "$RUN_DIR" [--dry-run]
   ```
   Exit codes as for the planning gate: 0 passed or dry run, 1 failing or `error` verdicts, 2 fatal. The script retries and shortens; do not re-run.
8. Point to the weak spot for each failing cell exactly as `anchor-plan-review` step 6, against `$W/item.txt`; here `change` says what the work or the sprint report should show. Then render: `python3 "$SCRIPT" report --run <run path> --format md`.
9. Collect `deterministic_checks`: for every result whose `verdict` is `satisfied` or `asserted_only` and whose `deterministic_check` is non-empty, emit `{anchor_id, verdict, check}`.
10. Return the envelope below. `item_id` is the effective item identifier in both modes; keep `sprint_id` equal to the legacy input in legacy mode, otherwise null. `results` copy the run's `results[]` unchanged plus `to_fix` on failing cells; `reused_run` is true when `run` was given. Measure `duration_ms`, count actual external tool calls, and derive `retry_count` from extra script attempts exactly as `anchor-plan-review` does; do not emit placeholder zeroes.

